# Secrets and local environment.
#
# The `**/` prefix matters. Vite reads apps/web/.env at build time, so a bare
# `.env` pattern that only reached the context root would let a developer's local
# file quietly bake an absolute API URL into the SPA and pull apps/api/.env,
# which holds the database credentials, into the build stage.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

